## 1. Purpose

This document consolidates the findings from the competitive research conducted for the SkyPath flight-booking experience.

The analysis covers five products representing different positions within the travel-booking ecosystem:

- Booking.com
- Google Flights
- Skyscanner
- Emirates
- Qatar Airways

Rather than comparing visual appearance alone, the analysis focuses on how each platform approaches:

- Flight discovery
- Comparison
- Price transparency
- Fare selection
- Flexibility
- Passenger information
- Ancillary services
- Booking completion
- Confirmation
- Post-booking management

The objective is to identify transferable interaction patterns and gaps that can inform the SkyPath design.

---

